          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Avoid being the last player holding cards after both phases.',
          gameplay: 'Phase one: all players play one card to each trick (from hand or stock). Suits do not matter; highest rank wins. Ties are broken by tied players playing again until one wins. After playing, each player draws from the stock to keep three cards until stock is empty. When a player has no card to play, phase one ends; players combine hand and won cards for phase two. Phase two: each turn beat the previous card or sequence, or pick up the lowest (earliest) card or sequence in the trick. Last player with cards loses.',
          keyRules: [
            'Phase One: Standard trick-taking, winner collects cards',
            'Phase Two: Beat the highest card showing or pick it up',
            'Suit ranking in Phase Two: Spades > Hearts > Diamonds > Clubs',
            'Last player with cards loses',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "In Phase One, try to win tricks to collect high cards for Phase Two, but don't collect too many cards. In Phase Two, save your highest cards for when you really need them.",
          intermediate: 'In Phase One, control when you win tricks - winning early tricks gives you control but also more cards to shed later. Try to collect cards in strong suits (Spades and Hearts).',
          advanced: "Card counting is crucial. Track which high cards have been played in Phase One to predict opponents' holdings in Phase Two. In Phase Two, force opponents to use their high cards early by playing medium cards that are difficult to beat without using premium cards.",
          tips: [
            "Don't win too many tricks in Phase One - each card won is a card you must shed in Phase Two",
            'Save Aces and Kings of Spades for critical moments in Phase Two',
            'Try to maintain cards in multiple suits to have flexibility in Phase Two',
            'If you have many low cards, consider picking up early in Phase Two to consolidate your hand',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
